The linker error `undefined reference to '__device_dts_ord_25'` indicates that a device object, likely related to the retention subsystem, is not being properly instantiated or linked. This often happens when a device tree node is referenced, but its corresponding driver is not enabled or the node itself is improperly defined.

In the provided `tests/subsys/settings/retention/boards/qemu_cortex_m3.overlay` file, the `retainedmem` node, which is intended to be a retained RAM region, is missing the `compatible = "zephyr,retained-ram"` property. This property is crucial for the Zephyr build system to identify the node as a `zephyr,retained-ram` device and enable the corresponding driver (`CONFIG_RETAINED_MEM_ZEPHYR_RAM`). Without this `compatible` property, the device object for `retainedmem` is not generated, leading to the linker error when the `retention` subsystem (which uses `settings_partition0` as its chosen node, a child of `retainedmem`) tries to access its underlying retained memory device.

Adding the `compatible` property will ensure that the `retainedmem` node is correctly recognized and its driver is enabled, resolving the linker error.

<tests/subsys/settings/retention/boards/qemu_cortex_m3.overlay>
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
		retainedmem {
			status = "okay";
			#address-cells = <1>;
			#size-cells = <1>;
			ranges;
========
		retainedmem {
			compatible = "zephyr,retained-ram";
			status = "okay";
			#address-cells = <1>;
			#size-cells = <1>;
			ranges;
